BasedOnStyle: LLVM
IndentWidth: 4
ColumnLimit: 200
NamespaceIndentation: All
FixNamespaceComments: true
SeparateDefinitionBlocks: Always
SortIncludes: Never
AllowShortBlocksOnASingleLine: Never
AllowShortEnumsOnASingleLine: false
AllowShortFunctionsOnASingleLine: None
AllowShortLambdasOnASingleLine: None
AllowShortLoopsOnASingleLine: false
AllowShortIfStatementsOnASingleLine: WithoutElse
# Project rule: if and if/else bodies always use braces, except a single continue or break may remain on the same line.
# Project rule: content within braces always starts on the following line.
# Project rule: DSL builder chains are vertically formatted, with every nested expression and chained call indented on its own line.
# Project rule: place all class/struct data members at the end of the definition, after methods; group related members together and separate groups with blank lines.
# Project rule: declare each class/struct data member in its own declaration, even when types match. Comma-separated variable declarations are only acceptable inside function bodies.
# These member organization rules require manual enforcement; clang-format does not move or split data member declarations.
